Text:
fearlessManager is a program. The 'single' manager receives the messages that fearlessMessage sends, one at a time.
The 'single' manager is the fearlessManager that holds the lock of single_manager_at_Port.lock, in the folder at the 'manager path'.
The 'manager path' is the path of a folder, the same for fearlessManager and for fearlessMessage.
projects.info is a file in the folder at the 'manager path', containing an Info serialized as defined in the fearless standard library; only fearlessManager writes projects.info.
The Info of projects.info is a ProjectsInfo.
fearlessManager answers "Applied\n" when fearlessManager$receive(Message) ends with no error, and "Refused\n" Error when fearlessManager$receive(Message) ends with error.
Errors are produced by notations notProjectsInfo(Base16) and lockFilesError(LockFile1 .. LockFilen), left undefined in the design.

Grammar:
LockFile ::= "no_manager.lock" | "single_manager_at_" Port ".lock"
Port ::= [1-9][0-9]*
ProjectsInfo ::= Infos.map("projects", Projects, "reserve", Extensions)
Projects ::= Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn)
Extensions ::= Infos.list(Extension1 .. Extensionn)
TypeNames ::= Infos.list(TypeName1 .. TypeNamen)
Project ::= Infos.map("path", TaggedText, "kind", Kind, "mains", TypeNames, "mounts", Mount, "attenuators", Attenuator)
Mount ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, ProjectName1 .. TypeNamen, ProjectNamen)
Attenuator ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, TypeNames1 .. TypeNamen, TypeNamesn)
Kind ::= "idle" | "code" | "dataRead" | "dataEdit"
Extension ::= OSExtension
ProjectName ::= [a-z_][a-z0-9_]*
TaggedText ::= \
  Base16                                 \
  | "Str:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn \
  | "UStr:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn
EscapedChar ::= [0-9A-Za-z +\-*/=<>,.;:()\[\]{}`'"!?@#$%^&_|~\\]

Well formedness:
in Port: the digits form a number smaller than 65536
in Extension: not in {"fearless", "ffile000"-"ffile999", "fapp000"-"fapp999"}
in Extensions: all Extension are disjoint
in Projects: no two Project with equal TaggedText
in Project: all TypeName in TypeNames are disjoint
in ProjectName: ProjectName ".fearless" is a ValidSegment
in TaggedText: starts with "Str:" only if the EscapedChars are the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless Str encoding a valid OS FS path
in TaggedText: starts with "UStr:" only if the EscapedChars are the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless UStr encoding a valid OS FS path, and p.isStr is False
in TaggedText: is a Base16 only if no Fearless UStr encodes the path it decodes to

Invariant:
At every moment, at most one fearlessManager is the 'single' manager.

Story:
A event fearlessManager starts
B action fearlessManager$start()

Define fearlessManager$start():
A fact No folder is at the 'manager path'
B action fearlessManager tries to create a folder at the 'manager path', holding the empty file no_manager.lock, and projects.info holding Infos.map("projects", Infos.list(), "reserve", Infos.list())
C action fearlessManager$start()

Define fearlessManager$start():
A fact The LockFiles in the folder at the 'manager path' are LockFile1 .. LockFilen, and n is not 1
B action fearlessManager$fatalError(lockFilesError(LockFile1 .. LockFilen))

Define fearlessManager$start():
A fact The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile, and a process holds the lock of LockFile
B action fearlessManager ends

Define fearlessManager$start():
A fact The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile, and no process holds the lock of LockFile
B action fearlessManager takes the lock of LockFile
C fact projects.info does not hold a ProjectsInfo, and Base16 encodes the path of projects.info
D action fearlessManager$fatalError(notProjectsInfo(Base16))

Define fearlessManager$start():
A fact The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile, and no process holds the lock of LockFile
B action fearlessManager takes the lock of LockFile
C fact projects.info holds a ProjectsInfo
D action fearlessManager listens for connections on the loopback address, on a port Port that the OS picks
E action fearlessManager renames LockFile to single_manager_at_Port.lock

Define fearlessManager$fatalError(Error):
A action fearlessManager shows a dialog with Error
B action The user closes the dialog
C action fearlessManager deletes the folder at the 'manager path'
D action fearlessManager ends

Story:
A event A connection to the 'single' manager arrives
B action fearlessManager sends a Greeting on the connection
C event fearlessManager reads Message "\n" from the connection
D action fearlessManager$receive(Message)
E action fearlessManager answers on the connection
F action fearlessManager ends the connection

Story:
A event A connection to the 'single' manager arrives
B action fearlessManager sends a Greeting on the connection
C event The connection ends, or fearlessManager reads from the connection a line that is not of form Message "\n"
D action fearlessManager ends the connection

Define fearlessManager$receive(EditMetadata Base16):
A if the file at Base16 does not hold a ProjectsInfo, error notProjectsInfo(Base16)
B action fearlessManager$write(the ProjectsInfo of the file at Base16)

Define fearlessManager$write(ProjectsInfo):
A action fearlessManager replaces projects.info with ProjectsInfo
B action fearlessManager tells the manager GUI, if the manager GUI runs, to read projects.info again

Implementation notes:
The 'manager path' is the folder fearless<version> next to the program folder, the folder holding fearlessManager and fearlessMessage.
fearlessManager creates the folder at the 'manager path' by filling a new folder next to the 'manager path', then renaming that new folder to the 'manager path': the rename fails when a folder is at the 'manager path' already.
The lock of a LockFile is the lock of FileChannel.tryLock: one call of FileChannel.tryLock finds that no process holds the lock and takes the lock; the OS releases the lock when the process ends, however the process ends, and the lock follows the file when the file is renamed.
fearlessManager sends the Greeting as soon as a connection arrives, also while fearlessManager$receive runs for another Message.
notProjectsInfo(Base16) could be triggered because the file does not exists, or because it exists and is not a valid info, or it is a valid info that is not a valid ProjectInfo, including all the well formedness. The error should investigate and report detail error informations, in the style of Frontend compile errors.
